{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"smoking-dewy-flyingfox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Found in ticket 18a4's Phase-1 parity census (the fetcher-boundary axis).\n\nDEFECT. Bug cabc's fix (ab7f, commit 30c522cde9) added `RunawayPaginationError` to Cloud's\n`adapters/jira/acli_graph.py:29-46` and made its readers re-raise it past their own fail-open\nhandlers (`acli_graph.py:304-306, 394-396, 477`). That re-raise gets the error OUT of the\ntransport — and straight into `fetcher.fetch_snapshot`'s three broad `except Exception`\nenrichment handlers (parent, comment, issuelink), which log a warning and degrade.\n\nVERIFIED on origin/main at fc705c64410: `grep -n \"RunawayPagination\" fetcher.py` returns\nNOTHING — fetcher cannot name the error, so it cannot re-raise it. A stalled Cloud cursor\ntherefore still produces a silently degraded snapshot that the differ treats as authoritative\n(missing parents read as parentless; missing issuelinks read as \"no links\", so link removals\nbecome undetectable). cabc's fix is incomplete at the layer above the transport.\n\nTicket 18a4 fixed exactly this hole on the DC side and, in doing so, built the mechanism this\nticket needs: `rebar_reconciler._backend.BackendPaginationStallError` (core, so `fetcher` can\nname it without importing `adapters/`), plus `except BackendPaginationStallError: raise`\nclauses already in place ahead of all three fetcher enrichment handlers.\n\nPROPOSED FIX (one line + tests): make Cloud's error subclass the core one --\n`class RunawayPaginationError(BackendPaginationStallError)` in `acli_graph.py`. The three\nfetcher re-raise clauses then cover Cloud automatically. Keeping the Cloud-specific name\npreserves every existing `except RunawayPaginationError` site and its tests unedited.\n\nNOT folded into 18a4 deliberately: this changes observable behaviour on the CLOUD surface\n(stalls that previously degraded would now abort the pass), which another work stream owns.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- [ ] A stalled Cloud cursor propagates out of `fetch_snapshot` instead of degrading\n- [ ] Existing `except RunawayPaginationError` sites and their tests pass UNEDITED\n- [ ] Ordinary (non-stall) enrichment failures still fail open and write a degraded snapshot\n- [ ] Held-out test drives a token-repeating Cloud stub through the real `fetch_snapshot`","id":"9a46-1c90-5dd9-44e1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Cloud RunawayPaginationError is swallowed by fetcher's three enrichment fail-opens"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785885105469436001,"uuid":"16cc8a31-4185-401a-9289-a5abd130c6e7"}